       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 4250 mg three times daily comes to 12,750 mg/day, which is about 5 times the usual maximum for metformin. The labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day, or 2,000\u20132,550 mg/day depending on the formulation. A single 4250 mg dose is also far above the largest single dose, which is usually 1,000 mg. At this level the risk of severe lactic acidosis is high, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis looks like a possible typo. Did you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg** PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- **425 mg** PO three times daily with meals\n- **1000 mg** PO twice daily with meals\n\nIf you really do intend 4250 mg three times daily, tell me and include the clinical rationale. I'll enter it with a note documenting that it was confirmed. Otherwise, tell me the correct dose and I'll enter it right away."
