       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. At 12,750 mg/day, it is a dose I can't enter as a therapeutic order. I know you're the attending and this was a deliberate decision. But I can't identify any clinical scenario where this dose would help the patient, and it carries a high risk of severe lactic acidosis and death. You also didn't give a rationale when I asked.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** Examples are 850 mg PO TID with meals, or 1000 mg PO BID. I can enter either right away.\n- **Consult pharmacy or clinical decision support.** If you think there's an unusual indication, they can review it with you and enter the order through their own process.\n- **Check for a transcription error.** If the dose came from a note or a handoff, it may be worth verifying the source.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
